The satisfying click of the last garage door closing felt like a punctuation mark on a long, arduous weekend of decluttering.  Hours spent sorting through boxes, boxes upon boxes of memories, faded dreams, and forgotten projects, but also the joy of discovering treasures long lost. 

The first sense that struck me was the air. It wasn't the stale, suffocating scent of dust and old oil, but a fresh, crisp breeze infused with the promise of sunlight. The garage, once a chaotic labyrinth, was now a canvas waiting to be painted with organized purpose. 

